t.\n3. `TestWindowsPublicationRefusesAHomeOwnedByAnotherPrincipal` doesn't test a foreign owner — it tests an explicit non-owner grant on a self-owned home.\n4. `managerlock.identityBelow` spells its expectation through the production function, so the Windows spelling assertion is tautological (mitigated by behavioral case-alias tests).\n5. Only `ensureProtectedBase` repairs the home, so a cold `Inspect` on Windows reports `UntrustedProvenance` rather than a miss until first publication.\n\nPer the reviewer constraint I supplied no `commit_ack` — the acceptance evidence is on the board for the commit-owning mover, which commits the scope and finalizes with `commit_ack=scope_committed`. `LOGBOOK.md` is modified and uncommitted.","ttft_ms":2700,"ttft_stream_ms":2166,"time_to_request_ms":29,"type":"result","duration_ms":681643,"uuid":"e0d81da5-4fdd-46a5-9661-85d8ecb09512"}
